   BEEUE; Int Clean Energy Talent Program; UNiLAB},
Abstract = {Building sun-shading design is an important aspect in new type
   energy-saving building technique. Based on the sun-shading and building
   integrated design case of a comprehensive teaching and laboratory
   building, we investigated the external shading and building integrated
   design practice in this paper. Indoor light and wind environment as well
   as energy-saving effects after setting external sun-shading device were
   analyzed by using simulation software. The results illustrated that the
   indoor thermal environment and comfort level could be highly improved
   through reasonable design of external sun-shading while the energy
   consumption of air conditioners was also reduced. This research offered
   direct reference for the building sun-shading project and promoted the
   sun shading and building integration design. Copyright (C) 2018 Elsevier
