Organization = {Slovak Acad Sci, Inst Landscape Ecol},
Abstract = {Many rivers of Ukraine and Europe such as Dnister, Tisza, and Prut run
   out from the Carpathians. Those are natural wealth of this land
   glorified in songs and legends which development shall be based on the
   past, present and future - nature and man in it. Nowadays nature and
   people are threatened. The poorly considerated construction of numerous
   small hydro power stations (SHPSs) in the Carpathians rivers poses this
   threat.
   A number of SHPSs are in the process of construction: Dzembronianska,
   Holoshynska, on the river Sarata (their construction stopped because of
   protests from the community) and near village Nyzhniy Bystryi. In
   addition, more than 500 SHPSs are at various stages of planning, design
   and issuing of permits in the Carpathian region of Ukraine.
   It should be noted that the planned SHPSs have a number of significant
   complex and cumulative environmental impacts. Such intensive development
   requires the strategic environmental assessment at the regional level to
   avoid irreversible damage of the fragile ecosystems of the Carpathians.
   The ``ecosystem approach{''} (EA) of CBD and IUCN resolution on dams and
   hydraulic infrastructure (2012) were considered as the methodological
   basis for a new generation of procedural documents on development of
   renewable energy sources in Ukraine.},
