   Buildings/3rd International Conference on Built Environment and Public
   Health, Guilin, PEOPLES R CHINA, MAY 29-31, 2009},
Organization = {Hunan Univ; Univ Hong Kong; Tsinghua Univ},
Abstract = {Based on the concept of ``Heat Island Effect{''}, the authors set
   several test sites in urban or suburb areas of Changsha and apply five
   DataRecorder testers to record the temperature and humidity of each site
   every one hour for confirming the existence of Heat Island Effect, Dry
   Island Effect and Wet Island Effect. Then the authors profoundly analyze
   the formation cause of Heat Island Effect in Changsha, and propose some
   feasible solutions and suggestions as follows: wide reforestation in the
   city; appropriate increase urban irrigation facilities; reasonable
   layout of urban structure; application of shallow-colored external
   decoration materials; control of the densities of urban population and
   architectures; progressive cancellation of small heating sources in
   residence communities and wide development of public transport.},
