Organization = {CNR, Grp Nazl Cibernet \& Biofis; Elsag Bailey; Reg Siciliana; Palermo
   Univ, Ctr Interdipt Tecnol Conoscenza; Pavia Univ, Ctr Interdipt Sci
   Cognit; Italian Presidency European Union 1996; ACM SIGARCH; ACM SIGART;
   ACM SIGCHI},
Abstract = {The discussion of this panel covered several aspects of data and
   information fusion in the context of pragmatic observation and
   evaluation. This summary tries to capture the major issues of the very
   lively panel discussion. Maximal originality of the statements has been
   tried to achieve by integrating original contributions not only of
   panellists but also of active participants. Besides the nine hot points
   prepared by the panellists one question dominated the discussion. Many
   participants argued strongly that models play a very important role in
   fusion for perception as well as in fusion in artificial systems. We
   therefore added as the 10th hot point: `Is there anything like
   model-free fusion?'},
