Abstract = {Twenty amusic and 20 control speakers of French were presented with
   pairs of Mandarin lexical tones to discriminate as same or different.
   Results revealed that even if the amusic group performed significantly
   below the control group, the scores of the two groups largely
   overlapped, with only 15\% of the amusic group performing outside the
   normal variations. Thus, the findings suggest a modest transfer of
   deficit between music and speech, which in turn calls for further work
   in order to identify the nature of the mediating factors.},
