   \& Hlth; Int Council Res \& Innovat Bldg \& Construct; European Commiss
   Asia Pro Eco Programme Promot Sustainable Solut Environm Europe \& Asia;
   Korean Soc Indoor Environm; Soc Indoor Environm},
Abstract = {The purpose of this study is to investigate current status and influence
   factors of indoor air pollution in Beijing. About 463 persons were
   chosen randomly to complete questionnaires. The levels of formaldehyde
   and NOx were monitored in bedrooms and kitchens of 91 households.
   Average daily concentration of formaldehyde in bedrooms was about 0.049
   mg/m(3) (over standard rate 13\%). Formaldehyde pollution in furnished
   rooms (0.058 mg/m(3)) was heavier than that in unfurnished rooms (0.034
   mg /m(3)) with statistically significant difference (P<0.001). Average
   concentrations of NOx in bedrooms and kitchens were 0.053 mg/m(3) and
   0.090 mg/m(3) (over standard rates 9\% and 48\% respectively) with
   statistically significant difference (p<0.001). We used multiple
   regression model to discover that house decoration was the most
   important factor on formaldehyde; natural gas was the primary source of
   NOx in kitchens and it was also an important source of formaldehyde in
   bedrooms; smoking was a main source of NOx in bedrooms.},
