Organization = {University College of Technology Sarawak; University of Edinburgh; RMIT
   University (RMITU); Northumbria University},
Abstract = {In this event we are interested to highlight the political dimensions of
   participatory design, by surfacing community-led and valuesdriven
   participatory design practices, more specifically in relation to
   solidarity, cooperativism and digital commons. We intend to do this in
   two events: The first event will be focused on bringing together
   cooperative organisations and communities across various sectors, and
   more specifically cultural spaces, energy, digital and urban commons,
   and cooperative economies to share opportunities and challenges of
   designing together differently. In addition to the creation of potential
   synergies and the sharing of knowledge at this first event, we
   anticipate that in addition to the Participatory Design Conference
   proceedings, this first event will create a knowledge base to be used
   for the participatory designing of the commoning practices of
   individuals and organisations active in producing digital commons in
   Greece (second event). As such, in addition to highlighting the
   political potential of Participatory Design and a call for
   ``democratizing innovation{''}, through this PDC Place, we aim to bring
   together and strengthen the participatory design and digital commons
   communities.},
