Year = {2023},
Pages = {819-836},
Note = {10th International Conference on Design Computing and Cognition (DCC),
   Univ Strathclyde, Glasgow, SCOTLAND, 2022},
Abstract = {The creation of distinct pattern designs (decorative geometric
   tessellations) has been studied at the level of geometric
   transformations and culture, but its link with emotional experience is
   less well established. This paper seeks to reverse engineer the creation
   of pattern by examining the emotive status of abstract forms, in this
   case lines. By firstly establishing how line, shape and symmetry are the
   key building blocks of pattern and exploring the links between emotion
   and visual perception, a study is presented intended to explore form
   expression within design and emotive meaning through the free-hand
   drawing of lines. The results of this study are then utilized to create
   a set of emotionally attuned pattern designs that are then subsequently
   analyzed in a separate study, establishing a link between form
   expression, emotional experience and pattern. These links are
   subsequently explored further and the implications for wider design
   practice and scholarship are discussed.},
