   PENNSYLVANIA, INST RES COGNIT SCI, PHILADELPHIA, PA, AUG 13-15, 2000},
Organization = {Cognit Sci Soc},
Abstract = {This paper describes an exemplar-based model of people's classification
   and typicality judgements in both single and combined categories. This
   model, called the diagnostic evidence model, explains the observed
   family resemblance structure of single categories; the productive nature
   of category combination; the observed overextension of typicality
   judgments in some combined categories; and the situations in which that
   overextension occurs. The model also gives a close fit to quantitative
   results from a representative single-category classification data-set.},
