   ANCHORAGE, AK, MAY 04-09, 1998},
Organization = {Int Neural Network Soc; IEEE, Neural Networks Council; IEEE, Alaska Sect},
Abstract = {A novel approach to the recognizing visual system synthesis is proposed
   The nonlinear net with continuous activating parameters representing
   positions of the perceived set of dots in the Euclidean space is
   developed an principles of geometrical invariant pattern formation. This
   net memorizes patterns by their relative location towards the system
   centroid point, that allows to distinguish objects that may be naturally
   realized fr om those impossible states. As an effect of the net basis
   the properties of distinctly moving dots gathering and resulting
   structure recognition in the indpendent coordinate space appear. At the
   same time the proposed model does not recognize individually moving dots
   as the structure if the motion is an accelerated process.},
