   Asia-Pacific-Society-of-Infection-Control, Singapore, SINGAPORE, MAR
   14-17, 2004},
Organization = {Asia Pacific Soc Infect Control},
Abstract = {Legionellosis is endemic in Singapore, with sporadic cases reported
   throughout the year. The absence of outbreak could be due to the low
   prevalence of the highly pathogenic Pontiac subtype of Legionella
   pneumophila in the urban environment. Mandatory maintenance of cooling
   towers and water fountains has been put in place, and the effectiveness
   of legislation in minimizing the occurrence and risk of outbreak of
   legionellosis is being evaluated.},
