Abstract = {This article discusses how poor people in Recife, in the northeast of
   Brazil, deal with everyday difficulties, using solidarity and the gift
   as resources to cope with needs which are extensive given the
   insufficiency and ineffectiveness of public policy, and how these
   practices and feelings are related to quality of life. Solidarity is
   structured according to the tripartite obligation to give, receive and
   reciprocate, on which the system of the gift is based. Knowledge of how
   such relations are established may help strengthen the organic and more
   sustainable forms that the excluded discover to achieve quality of life
   for themselves. (C) 2011 Published by Elsevier Ltd. Selection and
