Organization = {RAS, SB, CSBG, Lab Ecology \& Geobotany},
Abstract = {The coenopopulations of Bupleurum longifolium L., Pulmonaria mollis
   Wulf. ex Hornem., Angelica sylvestris L were studied in the territory of
   the experimental forest park of CSBG (Novosibirsk). The coenopopulations
   have a left-sided spectrum. The main method of reproduction of species -
   seed. In the intact pine-birch forest, coenopopulations of species with
   a low density of individuals develop. In weakly disturbed habitats
   (selective felling, periodic haying) the densities of individuals in B.
   longifolium, P. mollis increases, as well as old (in B. longifolium) or
   juvenile (in A. sylvestris) individuals fall out. Improving lighting
   here causes an increase in the size parameters of generative individuals
   and the acceleration of their development.},
